@ 29.2 - Proto-Na-Dene to Tlingit
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wikipedia contributors (2015), “Na-Dene languages”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. NB: Where a colon appears, forms to the left are the typical forms and forms to the right are “l-assimilated”. Somethings going on with the velars and uvulars; apparently, both the rounded and unrounded consonants have reflexes that may or may not be rounded
